y. The play was produced in 1914 on Broadway; it starred Lionel's younger brother John Barrymore and Florence Reed. The stage version played between January 20 and June 1914. The play was previously made into an American film \\\"The Yellow Passport\\\" in 1916\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e:d01\", \"text\": \"The Yellow Ticket (1918 film) The Yellow Ticket is a 1918 American silent drama film directed by William Parke and starring Fannie Ward. It is based on Michael Morton's 1914 play, \\\"The Yellow Ticket\\\". Anna Mirrel, a young Jewish girl in Czarist Russia, is forced to pretend to be a prostitute to obtain a passport (a \\\"yellow ticket\\\") in order to visit her father, whom she believes to be ill. When she arrives in St. Petersburg, she learns that her father has been killed. She encounters a young journalist and tells him of the crimes the state perpetrates against its\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [], \"prior_explanation\": \"I am uncertain about a specific film titled 'Yellow Ticket' with a widely known director. Without more context or a specific year, I cannot confirm the director.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Raoul Walsh\", \"scope\": \"Director of the 1931 film \\\"Yellow Ticket\\\"\", \"claim\": \"The 1931 pre-Code American drama film \\\"The Yellow Ticket\\\" was directed by Raoul Walsh.\", \"answer\": \"Raoul Walsh\", \"quote\": \"The Yellow Ticket The Yellow Ticket is a 1931 pre-Code American drama film based on the 1914 play of the same name by Michael Morton, produced by the Fox Film Corporation and directed by Raoul Walsh.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"William Parke\", \"scope\": \"Director of the 1918 film \\\"Yellow Ticket\\\"\", \"claim\": \"The 1918 American silent drama film \\\"The Yellow Ticket\\\" was 